{"id": 8194, "doi": "10.4038/slja.v25i1.8194", "title": "A case of yellow nail syndrome \u2013 Anaesthetic management and concerns", "abstract": "<p><span>A 19-year old patient diagnosed with yellow nail syndrome was posted for bronchoscopic examination for aspiration and clearance of secretions. There were symptoms pertaining to cardiorespiratory systems. He was uncooperative to undergo the procedure under local anaesthesia. Procedure was successfully managed using dexmedetomidine infusion.</span></p>", "keywords": ["Yellow nail syndrome", "respiratory distress", "bronchoscopy"], "authors": [{"first_name": "Shaji", "last_name": "Mathew", "institution": "Kasturba Medical College", "country": "IN", "email": "shajimanipal@yahoo.co.in", "orcid": ""}, {"first_name": "Jayanth A", "last_name": "Navada", "institution": "Kasturba Medical College", "country": "IN", "email": "", "orcid": ""}, {"first_name": "Arun Kumar", "last_name": "Handigodu Duggappa", "institution": "Kasturba Medical College", "country": "IN", "email": "", "orcid": ""}, {"first_name": "Shiyad", "last_name": "Mohamed", "institution": "Kasturba Medical College", "country": "IN", "email": "", "orcid": ""}], "section": "Case Reports", "pages": "53-55", "date_published": "2017-02-03T00:00:00+00:00", "date_submitted": "2016-11-04T13:22:35+00:00", "license_name": "", "license_link": "", "files": [{"label": "PDF", "language": "en", "url": "https://slja.sljol.info/articles/8194/files/8194-1-29504-1-10-20170203.pdf"}], "references": "", "volume": 25, "number": "1", "year": 2017, "issue_id": 735}